ARM64_TAGGED_ADDR_ABI	y	CPU extension, default y: detected per CPU at run time; the Cortex-A57 and A53 of the Exynos 5433 are ARMv8.0 and do not implement it. The tagged address syscall ABI: every ARMv8 CPU ignores the top byte of a user address, so this one does take effect: user space may pass pointers with a non-zero top byte
ARM64_TLB_RANGE	y	CPU extension, default y: detected per CPU at run time; the Cortex-A57 and A53 of the Exynos 5433 are ARMv8.0 and do not implement it
ARM64_USE_LSE_ATOMICS	y	CPU extension, default y: detected per CPU at run time; the Cortex-A57 and A53 of the Exynos 5433 are ARMv8.0 and do not implement it
ARM64_VA_BITS_52	y	arm64 default that our change replaces: 39 bits are enough (the owner's decision). Consequences: ARM64_PA_BITS_48, no ARM64_LPA2, 3 page-table levels instead of 5
