ARM_PSCI_FW	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: PSCI firmware support. None of it runs with the board's device tree: it has no psci node (the board dts deletes it: the bootloader offers no PSCI) and no enable-method
ARM_SMCCC_SOC_ID	y	new driver, built in by default: the SoC bus entry from ARM_SMCCC_SOC_ID. It returns at once while the firmware is known to report less than SMCCC 1.2, and on this board that is never asked (no SMCCC conduit: no psci node in the device tree)
