HW_RANDOM_ARM_SMCCC_TRNG	m	new driver, module by default (follows HW_RANDOM=m): a random number source behind the ARM SMCCC TRNG interface, i.e. a call into the secure monitor. udev would load it through its alias (platform:smccc_trng), but that device is registered by the built-in SMCCC discovery (drivers/firmware/smccc/smccc.c) only once it has found the interface in the firmware, and on this board the discovery never runs: PSCI is what starts it (drivers/firmware/psci), and the board's device tree has no psci node. So the module is never loaded and the firmware is never asked. The board's own generator is HW_RANDOM_EXYNOS (=m, unchanged)
IOMMU_API	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: DMA mapping through an IOMMU, selected by arm64. No IOMMU driver is built (EXYNOS_IOMMU is not set in the release and stays so)
IOMMU_DEFAULT_DMA_STRICT	y	default: strict DMA for IOMMUs
IOMMU_DMA	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: DMA mapping through an IOMMU, selected by arm64. No IOMMU driver is built (EXYNOS_IOMMU is not set in the release and stays so)
IOMMU_IOVA	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: DMA mapping through an IOMMU, selected by arm64. No IOMMU driver is built (EXYNOS_IOMMU is not set in the release and stays so)
IRQ_MSI_IOMMU	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: DMA mapping through an IOMMU, selected by arm64. No IOMMU driver is built (EXYNOS_IOMMU is not set in the release and stays so)
IRQ_MSI_LIB	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: DMA mapping through an IOMMU, selected by arm64. No IOMMU driver is built (EXYNOS_IOMMU is not set in the release and stays so)
KERNEL_MODE_NEON	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: the kernel may use the NEON registers (crypto, hashing). The release had it off, the arm32 default
LRU_GEN_WALKS_MMU	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
MITIGATE_SPECTRE_BRANCH_HISTORY	y	default y: the arm64 counterpart of the release's HARDEN_BRANCH_HISTORY. The firmware part of the workaround needs an SMCCC conduit, which only PSCI establishes and the board's device tree has no psci node to do so
MODULES_USE_ELF_RELA	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
NEED_SG_DMA_FLAGS	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
NEED_SG_DMA_LENGTH	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
NVIDIA_CARMEL_CNP_ERRATUM	y	erratum workaround, default y: matched against the CPU at run time, so it acts only on the listed core
OF_IOMMU	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: DMA mapping through an IOMMU, selected by arm64. No IOMMU driver is built (EXYNOS_IOMMU is not set in the release and stays so)
PARTITION_PERCPU	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
POSIX_CPU_TIMERS_TASK_WORK	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
PTP_1588_CLOCK_KVM	y	new driver, built in by default: a PTP clock for KVM guests. It only tests a cached bitmap that is filled under a hypervisor (HVC conduit), so it does nothing here and makes no firmware call
QCOM_FALKOR_ERRATUM_1003	y	erratum workaround, default y: matched against the CPU at run time, so it acts only on the listed core
QCOM_FALKOR_ERRATUM_1009	y	erratum workaround, default y: matched against the CPU at run time, so it acts only on the listed core
QCOM_FALKOR_ERRATUM_E1041	y	erratum workaround, default y: matched against the CPU at run time, so it acts only on the listed core
QCOM_QDF2400_ERRATUM_0065	y	erratum workaround, default y: matched against the CPU at run time, so it acts only on the listed core
QUEUED_RWLOCKS	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
QUEUED_SPINLOCKS	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
RANDOMIZE_KSTACK_OFFSET	y	default y: a random offset in the kernel stack at each system call
RELOCATABLE	y	default y: the Image applies its own relocations, so it starts wherever it is loaded. Needed by the loader, which copies the Image into a slot
RELR	y	default y: relocations packed in the RELR format (the toolchain supports it)
ROCKCHIP_ERRATUM_3588001	y	erratum workaround, default y: matched against the CPU at run time, so it acts only on the listed core
RODATA_FULL_DEFAULT_ENABLED	y	default y: the kernel's read-only data is also read-only through the direct mapping. The release had STRICT_KERNEL_RWX on arm32
RUSTC_SUPPORTS_ARM64	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
SECRETMEM	y	default y: memfd_secret()
SOCIONEXT_SYNQUACER_PREITS	y	erratum workaround, default y: matched against the CPU at run time, so it acts only on the listed core
SPARSEMEM	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: the sparse memory model and its virtual memmap (arm64 has no flat memory model)
SPARSEMEM_EXTREME	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: the sparse memory model and its virtual memmap (arm64 has no flat memory model)
SPARSEMEM_VMEMMAP	y	default y: the memmap of the sparse memory model in a virtual mapping
SPARSEMEM_VMEMMAP_ENABLE	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: the sparse memory model and its virtual memmap (arm64 has no flat memory model)
SPLIT_PMD_PTLOCKS	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
SURFACE_PLATFORMS	y	default y: a menu (drivers of Microsoft Surface devices); empty here
SYSCTL_EXCEPTION_TRACE	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
TIME_NS	y	default y: CLONE_NEWTIME
TOOLS_SUPPORT_RELR	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice: the toolchain packs relocations in the RELR format
TRACE_IRQFLAGS_NMI_SUPPORT	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
UNMAP_KERNEL_AT_EL0	y	default y: the kernel is unmapped from the user page tables on CPUs affected by Meltdown; decided per CPU at run time
USER_STACKTRACE_SUPPORT	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
VDSO_GETRANDOM	y	no prompt: a capability flag that the arm64 architecture, or its toolchain check, selects. Not a choice
ZONE_DMA	y	default y on arm64: ZONE_DMA covers the memory below 4 GiB, ZONE_DMA32 is empty
ZONE_DMA32	y	default y on arm64: ZONE_DMA covers the memory below 4 GiB, ZONE_DMA32 is empty
